# Design System: Material Design 3

This project uses **[Material Design 3](https://m3.material.io/)** as the only design system. All UI, layout, motion, and visual decisions must follow M3 — not Material 2, not an ad-hoc style.

## Source of truth

Before creating or restyling UI, read the matching page on [m3.material.io](https://m3.material.io/):

- Foundations: tokens, accessibility, interaction states, layout
- Styles: [color](https://m3.material.io/styles/color/overview), [typography](https://m3.material.io/styles/typography/overview), [shape](https://m3.material.io/styles/shape/overview), [elevation](https://m3.material.io/styles/elevation/overview), [motion](https://m3.material.io/styles/motion/overview), [icons](https://m3.material.io/styles/icons/overview)
- Components: use the official M3 component (name, variants, anatomy) instead of inventing one

## Stack

- Next.js + React + Tailwind v4
- Express M3 with CSS tokens (`--md-sys-*`) and custom React components
- Do **not** install `@material/web` unless the user explicitly asks (maintenance mode; not a React library)

## Typefaces (do not replace)

Font families are already defined in `app/globals.css`. Reuse them; never introduce Roboto or other M3 default typefaces.

- **Titles** (display / headline / title): `var(--font-serif)` / `font-serif`
- **Body** (body / label): `var(--font-sans)` / `font-sans`
- **Code**: `var(--font-mono)` / `font-mono`

M3 typescale tokens may set size, weight, line-height, and tracking only. `--md-sys-typescale-*-font` and `--md-ref-typeface-*` must point at those same CSS variables.

## Hard rules

- Color, type, shape, and elevation come from tokens — never raw one-off hex/px in components
- Pair every fill with its `on-*` color (accessible contrast)
- Elevation is primarily **tonal surface**, not drop shadows
- Interactive elements need M3 states: enabled, hovered, focused, pressed, disabled
- Prefer M3 names in code (`TopAppBar`, `FilledCard`, `FilledTonalButton`) so the mapping stays obvious
